// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// knc_check_orchestrate — Typecheck an orchestrate declaration
//
// An orchestrate block declares a multi-stage computation graph with:
//   - Stage bindings, each typed by runtime kind (cpu, gpu, law, etc.)
//   - Optional metadata per stage:
//       * when target/capability selectors
//       * after / deps for dependency ordering
//       * residency (host, shared, device) + transfer (none, host_to_device, etc.)
//       * guarded by <axiom> — capability-gated execution
//       * fallback abort/<stage>/degrade <stage>
//       * requires <law_stage>
//       * policy static/telemetry_prefer_gpu/...
//   - A body block with local statements and a return expression
//
// Validation the spec-layer will add:
//   - Stage runtime kind validation (0-11, ERR_ORCHESTRATE_UNKNOWN_RUNTIME)
//   - Duplicate stage name detection (ERR_ORCHESTRATE_DUPLICATE_STAGE)
//   - Dependency resolution (each dep must be a declared stage)
//   - Guard is-axiom check (guarded by must reference axiom, not fn)
//   - Requires is-stage check (requires must reference law stage)
//   - Fallback target resolution
//   - Transfer/residency compatibility matrix
//   - Cycle detection via DFS (ERR_ORCHESTRATE_CYCLE_DETECTED)
//   - Body block type inference vs declared return type
//
// Current status: STUB — returns TypedItem with i64 return type.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

